Presence: disconnect handler wipes a user who is already back online

Repro (probe against a local `npm run dev`, sanjarb @ d7f9aca):

  1. socket A1 -> user:online "user-aaa"      => ["user-aaa"]
  2. socket B  -> user:online "user-bbb"      => ["user-aaa","user-bbb"]
  3. "user-aaa" reloads the page:
     socket A2 -> user:online "user-aaa"      => ["user-aaa","user-bbb"]   OK
  4. the OLD socket A1 finally drops          => ["user-bbb"]              BUG

After step 4 "user-aaa" is gone from the online set even though socket A2 is
connected and owns the mapping. Everyone — including that user's own client —
shows them offline. This fires on every page reload, every HMR reload and every
network blip, because socket.io reports the old socket's disconnect only after
the new one has already registered.

Cause: `disconnect` deletes by userId without checking whether this socket is
still the one the map points at.

Fix: only clear presence when this socket still owns the mapping.

--- a/src/index.js
+++ b/src/index.js
@@ -302,11 +302,15 @@
   // ── Disconnect ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   socket.on('disconnect', () => {
     console.log('User disconnected:', socket.id)
-    if (socket.userId) {
+    // Only clear presence if THIS socket still owns the mapping. On a reload
+    // the new socket registers first and the old one disconnects afterwards,
+    // so deleting unconditionally wipes a user who is plainly online.
+    if (socket.userId && onlineUsers.get(socket.userId) === socket.id) {
       onlineUsers.delete(socket.userId)
       io.emit('users:online', Array.from(onlineUsers.keys()))
     }
   })
 })

 app.get('/', (req, res) => {
   res.send('Server ishlayapti 🚀')
 })

The same stale-socket assumption also affects message delivery: `onlineUsers`
is what `chat:send` looks up for `chat:receive` (index.js:261), so between the
reload and the next re-announce the recipient silently receives nothing. The
guard above fixes that path too.
